ion/math-academy-id "q-79841" :question/problem "Estimate $\\sqrt{3.9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.2)$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ at the point $(4,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(4,1),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡1}{2\\sqrt{4}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{\\sqrt{4}}{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =0\\,\\text{d}x+2\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(4+Δx,1+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈0\\,Δx+2\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3.9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.2)=f(3.9,1.2),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(3.9,1.2).$\n\nMoving from $(4,1)$ to $(3.9,1.2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =3.9-4=-0.1, \\\\ Δy & =1.2-1=0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈0\\cdot (-0.1)+2\\cdot (0.2) \\\\  & ≈0+0.4 \\\\  & ≈0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.4.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.9,1.2) & ≈f(4,1)+0.4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3.9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.2) & ≈\\sqrt{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+0.4 \\\\  & ≈0+0.4 \\\\  & ≈0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79841/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acafc931-a294-5ca7-8e39-cf8be29f08a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79841"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79959/selection/d82caaf964689d4c912c051dd06bb8ed286ca5df4e4545ffa136bd2c6ac80369" :answer/id #uuid "cfd052b9-a6fe-584b-9027-7713b15dec89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+6\\pi \\,\\text{d}l" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79959/selection/930777decaaf379708136459db015b8bdf31f8cc9ddbb87d8c51efde206b50b9" :answer/id #uuid "d64c152a-3ab7-5900-8f79-669eace39a62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,\\text{d}r+6\\,\\text{d}l" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79959/selection/a805042776902b71999844439dce122f37cc0ede240a889bb57e4819a49256bf" :answer/id #uuid "b5b38237-ffab-5541-8279-f2df4c28b930" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+12\\pi \\,\\text{d}l" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79959/selection/6fae0e63deb744171ad8e4574f18e9ca980b70326c228d8266acaf09f7331f33" :answer/id #uuid "40c33fc4-2139-5b3c-8fc6-7729768ac716" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{d}r+40\\,\\text{d}l" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79959/selection/813ded26a8ea0cc93e2cb997b3cd94d3295dbd664bf522af76f112d278d309e8" :answer/id #uuid "72e6ee56-8a8e-50dd-b580-d600702e778f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+10\\pi \\,\\text{d}l" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79959/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "015af702-09d0-5695-98c5-7791d87a48f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79959/selection/d82caaf964689d4c912c051dd06bb8ed286ca5df4e4545ffa136bd2c6ac80369" :answer-field/choices ["q-79959/selection/d82caaf964689d4c912c051dd06bb8ed286ca5df4e4545ffa136bd2c6ac80369" "q-79959/selection/930777decaaf379708136459db015b8bdf31f8cc9ddbb87d8c51efde206b50b9" "q-79959/selection/a805042776902b71999844439dce122f37cc0ede240a889bb57e4819a49256bf" "q-79959/selection/6fae0e63deb744171ad8e4574f18e9ca980b70326c228d8266acaf09f7331f33" "q-79959/selection/813ded26a8ea0cc93e2cb997b3cd94d3295dbd664bf522af76f112d278d309e8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79959" :question/id #uuid "ddfbfeb1-47d1-5e4a-929c-ad72e52c8b4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-79959" :question/problem "Given a right cone, find the differential $\\text{d}S$ for the lateral surface area $S$ of the right cone if the base radius is $r=6,$ and the slant height is $l=10.$" :question/worked-solution "The  lateral surface area of the right cone is $S=\\pi rl.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(rl) & =(\\frac{∂S}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂S}{∂l})\\,\\text{d}l \\\\  & =\\pi l\\,\\text{d}r+\\pi r\\,\\text{d}l\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=6,$ and $l=10,$  the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(6,10) & =10\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+6\\pi \\,\\text{d}l.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79959/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "153739f2-df62-5baf-8438-225edfc33ecb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79959"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
